95,475
VERDICT: BLOCK

1. Tombstone guard is still raceable: V1.2 specifies pre-SELECT then INSERT, but not one transaction/single writer closure. A concurrent `reject_link` between them lets classifier/backfill/DriveMetadata recreate an active row after tombstone.

2. User-relink carve-out is API-mismatched: §7 proves `add_link(..., UserRelink)` resurrects, but §10 says W4-A calls `override_link`; `override_link` has no attribution_source and no specified tombstone/create semantics.

3. Idempotency is only completion-time, not attempt-time: unique `WHERE status='success'` permits duplicate `in_progress` runs for the same key; duplicate work can execute before `complete_run` hits UNIQUE.

4. UPSERT syntax itself is SQLite-correct: `ON CONFLICT (...) WHERE rejected = 0 DO NOTHING RETURNING link_id` matches the partial unique index.
